{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation","id":1070875,"title":"Mage: the Desolation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-30T15:07:05-07:00","id":1070875,"title":"Mage: the Desolation","content":"I know that Mage has its own setting and all but I was wondering if it could be adapted to a Post Apocalyptic world where there is desolation everywhere and even magic can't always protect themselves as there are now bigger abd nastier stuff out there..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T15:16:30-07:00","id":1070880,"title":"","content":"I don't see why not. How desolate do you want it?<br /> <br /> I mean, I was thinking that a lot of the more depressing settings would actually be really good for mage. I mean, being a mage would allow you to somewhat ignore the constraints that a normal person would have to deal with. You can wander the ruins of a dead world without needing to worry too much about finding food for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T15:21:39-07:00","id":1070884,"title":"","content":"The power of the Arcana is such that if you don't do a heavy overhaul of the game's mechanics (in which case why use Mage as a starting point anyway), you're probably going to end up with characters as shadow rulers behind warlords and chieftains, shepherding your own power bases and settlements against whatever rival threats populate the wastelands. Almost like a tabletop game of Civilization to an extent, I imagine, as you'll need to be building up infrastructure that doesn't depend on you personally showing up and blessing everything all the time.<br /> <br /> That's not to say that's a bad outcome, just that if you're expecting a hardscrabble world, mage characters will probably be insulated from the worst of it.<br /> <br /> Interesting exercise to imagine how the Sleeping Curse would limit mages in this environment, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T15:48:36-07:00","id":1070897,"title":"","content":"if your intent is to strike home how the apocalypse left even mages desolate. you'll have to elaborate on the details. your average Mad Max or Fallout wasteland doesn't inherently have mages, so the question becomes how did the apocalypse effect magic?<br /> did the abyss come through?<br /> do the Exarchs have more power?<br /> are there Thaumaturvores running wild?<br /> is paradox stronger, more dangerous?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T15:50:00-07:00","id":1070899,"title":"","content":"There's are options, like making Anshos really common and more mobile, or lots of Abyssal stuff, increasing rates of Banishers and the condition more virulent, making it easier to become Mad, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T15:53:55-07:00","id":1070901,"title":"","content":"I would check out the Dark Sun setting for DnD, it has a good feel of magic being problematic in a apocalyptic like setting. You'd have to adapt it away from fantasy to contemporary/future of course.<br /> <br /> It would work well with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> 's increase in abyssal stuff and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar252_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"252\" data-vbnamecard=\"252\">basketcase</a> 's stronger paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T16:42:00-07:00","id":1070921,"title":"","content":"Well the setting that I was thinking of was where Mages caused the destruction of the earth in a Fire and Brimstone battle, and the sleepers know this. Mages are scarce as they are hunted, There are few hollows that do not produce Paradax laced Mana and those are patrolled by sleepers and beasts alike. There are hazards such as what is referred to as Mage Storms that will reveal anything or anyone that has a store of Mana in them, so get caught out in one of those storms and you could be exposed. If you decide that tainted Mana will do and you absorb it to fuel your magic, bad things happen as paradox is prevalent in everything you do while that Mana is in you. So having it easy in this world because you are a Mage isn't actually how I would put it.<br /> <br /> Then there are Mages that wander the bad land driven mad with the Paradox tainted Mana that will hunt you, There are dead zones that most of the remaining populace will congregate in because it is Magic free. the more Pure you are, None Tainted, the stronger your magic but it would be easier to spot you as a Mage.<br /> <br /> Something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 03-30-2017, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T16:55:23-07:00","id":1070926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1070921#post1070921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the setting that I was thinking of was where Mages caused the destruction of the earth in a Fire and Brimstone battle, and the sleepers know this. Mages are scarce as they are hunted, There are few hollows that do not produce Paradax laced Mana and those are patrolled by sleepers and beasts alike. There are hazards such as what is referred to as Mage Storms that will reveal anything or anyone that has a store of Mana in them, so get caught out in one of those storms and you could be exposed. If you decide that tainted Mana will do and you absorb it to fuel your magic, bad things happen as paradox is prevalent in everything you do while that Mana is in you. So having it easy in this world because you are a Mage isn't actually how I would put it.<br /> <br /> Then there are Mages that wander the bad land driven mad with the Paradox tainted Mana that will hunt you, There are dead zones that most of the remaining populace will congregate in because it is Magic free. the more Pure you are, None Tainted, the stronger your magic but it would be easier to spot you as a Mage.<br /> <br /> Something like taht.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, my question with this is what about all of the other ways of getting Mana <i>other</i> than Hallows? I mean Hallows are neither the best nor the easiest ways that mages in 2e can restore their personal Mana reserves, they just happen to be the only way other than Prime to get Tass in order to be able to carry around excess Mana (well that and Artifacts). And if this was really an end of the world type deal are Sleepers, having been as devastated as anyone else, <i>really</i> that big of a threat here? I doubt <i>all</i> of the Masters and Adepts are gone, and even 2 in an arcana can pretty easily cloak you from notice when it comes to mundane senses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T17:05:15-07:00","id":1070932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1070921#post1070921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the setting that I was thinking of was where Mages caused the destruction of the earth in a Fire and Brimstone battle, and the sleepers know this. Mages are scarce as they are hunted, There are few hollows that do not produce Paradax laced Mana and those are patrolled by sleepers and beasts alike. There are hazards such as what is referred to as Mage Storms that will reveal anything or anyone that has a store of Mana in them, so get caught out in one of those storms and you could be exposed. If you decide that tainted Mana will do and you absorb it to fuel your magic, bad things happen as paradox is prevalent in everything you do while that Mana is in you. So having it easy in this world because you are a Mage isn't actually how I would put it.<br /> <br /> Then there are Mages that wander the bad land driven mad with the Paradox tainted Mana that will hunt you, There are dead zones that most of the remaining populace will congregate in because it is Magic free. the more Pure you are, None Tainted, the stronger your magic but it would be easier to spot you as a Mage.<br /> <br /> Something like taht.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, cool, cool.<br /> <br /> merely some food for thought.<br /> how will Paradox Mana work?<br /> are you planning on lessening the other ways to gain mana?<br /> what makes sleepers so dangerous, that merely being reveled as a mage is a threat?<br /> Are you going to increase the mana cost for spell use?<br /> What are these Beast that are running around?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T17:07:46-07:00","id":1070934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1070921#post1070921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the setting that I was thinking of was where Mages caused the destruction of the earth in a Fire and Brimstone battle, and the sleepers know this.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more tricky. Powerful magic in mage tends to be of the order that you destory the ontology of your enemy. You can mess around with setting to fit it, but it won't be terribly neat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages are scarce as they are hunted, There are few hollows that do not produce Paradax laced Mana and those are patrolled by sleepers and beasts alike. There are hazards such as what is referred to as Mage Storms that will reveal anything or anyone that has a store of Mana in them, so get caught out in one of those storms and you could be exposed. </div> </div> </div>You'll need something to even the playing field. Hunters with modern weaponry struggle against the Awakened, the post-apocalypse makes that problem worse. Unless you do something about it your players are going to be laying waste to these hunters. (I guess you could wear them down through wisdom lose but that would require your sleeper population to be made up of fanatics who are willing to die to attack a group who aren't necessarily doing anything to them.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are dead zones that most of the remaining populace will congregate in because it is Magic free. the more Pure you are, None Tainted, the stronger your magic but it would be easier to spot you as a Mage. </div> </div> </div>I imagine not a few magi would quite like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T17:23:50-07:00","id":1070942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1070926#post1070926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, my question with this is what about all of the other ways of getting Mana <i>other</i> than Hallows? I mean Hallows are neither the best nor the easiest ways that mages in 2e can restore their personal Mana reserves, they just happen to be the only way other than Prime to get Tass in order to be able to carry around excess Mana (well that and Artifacts). And if this was really an end of the world type deal are Sleepers, having been as devastated as anyone else, <i>really</i> that big of a threat here? I doubt <i>all</i> of the Masters and Adepts are gone, and even 2 in an arcana can pretty easily cloak you from notice when it comes to mundane senses.</div> </div> </div> </div>These hunters are using devices that are high in Paradox and magic sensitive senses, so not everyone is using Mundane senses. the dead zones are a particular hazard. Living in a dead zone will protect you from being noticed but will also separate you from your magic, a fine line that some might choose to explore they can step out of the zone to resume being a Mage.<br /> <br /> In a dead zone it is an affect similar to the third stage of Souless &quot;Thrall&quot; a mage can not cast magic, Objects manufactures in a dead zone can be made to carry the same properties as that dead zone, get caught by a sleeper that is using one of these objects and see just how frightened of a sleeper you can become. Most of the masters that participated in the battle that destroyed the earth was also destroyed and those that survived are smart enough to hide.<br /> <br /> I don't want to make it so that a Mage is instantly exposed to all that see them but there would be enough hazards that a smart mage would be <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">cautious</span>. the main enemy wouldn't be the sleepers they are more dangerous then sleepers in that core setting the real danger is other mages.The Mage rules that kept a civilized face on magic is no more, No Concilium, no organized groups, it would be a dog eat dog world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T17:36:10-07:00","id":1070950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>basketcase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1070932#post1070932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cool, cool, cool.<br /> <br /> merely some food for thought.<br /> how will Paradox Mana work?<br /> are you planning on lessening the other ways to gain mana?<br /> what makes sleepers so dangerous, that merely being reveled as a mage is a threat?<br /> Are you going to increase the mana cost for spell use?<br /> What are these Beast that are running around?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>how will Paradox Mana work? </b>All spells that you cast while you have Paradox laced Mana in you will automatically produce Paradox dice equal to the taint of your Mana, if 5 of your 12 Mana is Paradox laced then every spell will has 5 dice of Paradox to deal with + all of the other Paradox stuff.<br /> <b>are you planning on lessening the other ways to gain mana? </b>Somewhat but I haven't figured out how I will do that yet.<br /> <b>what makes sleepers so dangerous, that merely being reveled as a mage is a threat?</b> The general populace isn't the threat most would run from you, they see you and they will alert the Hunters.<br /> <b>Are you going to increase the mana cost for spell use?</b> Yes<br /> <b>What are these Beast that are running around?</b> Think of something equivalent to a Paradox infused Werewolf that is sensitive to Mana stored in a person. Stuff like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1070934#post1070934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's more tricky. Powerful magic in mage tends to be of the order that you destory the ontology of your enemy. You can mess around with setting to fit it, but it won't be terribly neat.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the trickier part and I just started to hatch this Idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1070934#post1070934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll need something to even the playing field. Hunters with modern weaponry struggle against the Awakened, the post-apocalypse makes that problem worse. Unless you do something about it your players are going to be laying waste to these hunters. (I guess you could wear them down through wisdom lose but that would require your sleeper population to be made up of fanatics who are willing to die to attack a group who aren't necessarily doing anything to them.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Items that are travelling Dead Zones, is the start and I would be thinking of more.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1070934#post1070934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine not a few magi would quite like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not liked by most mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 03-30-2017, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T17:42:39-07:00","id":1070953,"title":"","content":"Hmm, play Sundered World? What'd be the difference between the Dawn of Civilization and it's end, technological-wise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T17:45:30-07:00","id":1070954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1070942#post1070942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> These hunters are using devices that are high in Paradox and magic sensitive senses, so not everyone is using Mundane senses. the dead zones are a particular hazard. Living in a dead zone will protect you from being noticed but will also separate you from your magic, a fine line that some might choose to explore they can step out of the zone to resume being a Mage.<br /> <br /> In a dead zone it is an affect similar to the third stage of Souless &quot;Thrall&quot; a mage can not cast magic, Objects manufactures in a dead zone can be made to carry the same properties as that dead zone, get caught by a sleeper that is using one of these objects and see just how frightened of a sleeper you can become. Most of the masters that participated in the battle that destroyed the earth was also destroyed and those that survived are smart enough to hide.<br /> <br /> I don't want to make it so that a Mage is instantly exposed to all that see them but there would be enough hazards that a smart mage would be <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">cautious</span>. the main enemy wouldn't be the sleepers they are more dangerous then sleepers in that core setting the real danger is other mages.<b>The Mage rules that kept a civilized face on magic is no more, No Concilium, no organized groups, it would be a dog eat dog world.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>This seems like it is going to end up like Dark Sun, where large swathes of land is going to be ruled by various all powerful sorcerer kings. I can't see Hunters being more than a nuisance to be hunted down as things quickly become a magocracy, where magic users wield their semi-phenomenal nearly cosmic power to bring order to and rule over the better parts of the wastelands. Though, to be fair, given the post-apocalyptic nature of the proposed setting it might actually be for the best. They could pretty easily provide food, water, and shelter for all who decide to step in line. Seems like a Seers win (kinda) situation actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T17:47:43-07:00","id":1070956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1070953#post1070953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, play Sundered World? What'd be the difference between the Dawn of Civilization and it's end, technological-wise?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Han't thought of just editing that in some way. I will look at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T17:51:31-07:00","id":1070958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Items that are travelling Dead Zones, is the start and I would be thinking of more. </div> </div> </div>That sounds kinda overpowered. A dead zone is very all or nothing. I dunno, but I wouldn't be surprised if your players roll their eyes everytime some sleepers turn up with such an item.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1070950#post1070950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not liked by most mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring more to the sleepers living where magi wouldn't want to go anyway. Quite a few of the Orders like sleepers to keep away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T17:53:28-07:00","id":1070959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1070954#post1070954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems like it is going to end up like Dark Sun, where large swathes of land is going to be ruled by various all powerful sorcerer kings. I can't see Hunters being more than a nuisance to be hunted down as things quickly become a magocracy, where magic users wield their semi-phenomenal nearly cosmic power to bring order to and rule over the better parts of the wastelands. Though, to be fair, given the post-apocalyptic nature of the proposed setting it might actually be for the best. They could pretty easily provide food, water, and shelter for all who decide to step in line. Seems like a Seers win (kinda) situation actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Until I get a better handle on the setting I can't say that it wouldn't turn out that way, But I don't see it like that, an that is not that setting that I imagined so it shouldn't turn out like that. The advantage of bringing it here first is to get an Idea of the pitfalls and the issues so as to work around them and make it the setting that I envisioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T17:58:01-07:00","id":1070960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1070959#post1070959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Until I get a better handle on the setting I can't say that it wouldn't turn out that way, But I don't see it like that, an that is not that setting that I imagined so it shouldn't turn out like that. The advantage of bringing it here first is to get an Idea of the pitfalls and the issues so as to work around them and make it the setting that I envisioned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Long story short, unless you gut the magic system somehow, I don't see it turning out any other way. Mage arcana are super potent, so potent that mundane people in a post apocalyptc setting aren't really going to stand a chance. And given that there's no body of mages to really keep their own in line it's likely going to degenerate into various mini-kingdoms ruled by the most powerful mages and those that follow them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T18:43:28-07:00","id":1070973,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> I wouldn't worry about your setting turning out anyway other then the way you imagine it.<br /> <br /> you seem to have a good idea for your alternate setting, do you know what you want the plot to be? an escape to a better land? overthrowing a sleeper kingdom? finding a great artifact that will fix history. <br /> Or are you just planning on playing in a loose sandbox maybe lots of little stories?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T19:08:19-07:00","id":1070985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1070960#post1070960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Long story short, unless you gut the magic system somehow, I don't see it turning out any other way. Mage arcana are super potent, so potent that mundane people in a post apocalyptc setting aren't really going to stand a chance. And given that there's no body of mages to really keep their own in line it's likely going to degenerate into various mini-kingdoms ruled by the most powerful mages and those that follow them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't really need to gut the magic system to make magic unreliable, adding mitigating factors would do more than enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T19:53:48-07:00","id":1070996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1070953#post1070953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, play Sundered World? What'd be the difference between the Dawn of Civilization and it's end, technological-wise?</div> </div> </div> </div>Better cars, poorer taste in clothing.<br /> <hr /><br /> Leveraging the Abyss is probably the best bet - say Something Happened, and now Abyssal horrors run amok... kinda. They need Paradox to be active, which means either idiots poking their noses where they shouldn't, or Mages being wasteful with magic/Mana. Maybe look to how Pandorans from Promethean operate in relation to the Created.<br /> <br /> Sure, your magic confers nice powers, but it draw monsters and someone is going to have to pay for your excesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T21:58:43-07:00","id":1071044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1070985#post1070985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't really need to gut the magic system to make magic unreliable, adding mitigating factors would do more than enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly sure I'd consider that gutting the magic system. As it stands I consider what we've got pretty much the ideal system of magic. It could probably be tuned slightly, but any change big enough to change the foreseen outcome is probably going to be enough to ruin it. I mean I'm sure some people wont mind, after all, some people like <i>vancian casting</i> for gods sake. But again, making it unreliable enough to matter is going to gut the system and take away part of what makes the mechanics of the gameline as good as it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T04:06:49-07:00","id":1071170,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2309\" data-vbnamecard=\"2309\">Ashenrogue</a> you don't like the Idea and that is fine not every setting is for everyone. I am confident that I can prevent your &quot;Only Possible Outcome&quot; scenario without gutting the system. So we will just have to agree to disagree. Also there is not reason why there couldn't be a few places that a mage has embedded himself on a throne to rule or is the power behind the throne of a community. That scenario would be the exception not the rule.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> The Abyss would play heavily into the setting, both as a source for beasts to challenge the mages and as a source to make spellcasting more hazardous.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, sans-serif\"> The only place that magic would be unreliable is in Abyss Zones (Abyss saturated) and it wouldn't work in Dead Zones at all. The only magic restriction that I can see would need to come in the form of Changing the History, need something as the plot of the story. Time as a whole would stay the same just spells that would have a lasting effect on Changing History,</span><br /> <br /> \u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar252_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"252\" data-vbnamecard=\"252\">basketcase</a> I was looking at the characters being fairly powerful in their own right (landing somewhere between 20 and 35 experience) and they are trying to find an artifact that will Rewrite History, but the Abyss is happy with it's new hold on the world and it doesn't want to give it up.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar178_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"178\" data-vbnamecard=\"178\">Michael</a> Maybe I overstated it. Some Items would carry the Dead Zone with them, they are difficult to make and the material would need to be perfected so not easy to come by, But large Hunting parties could possibly have one. The Hunters are only one part of the way to introduce danger to Mages, The Abyss, Other Mages, Beasts and Nature itself are other elements of the danger. The sleepers have placed Mages as the Villains of the setting and the characters are trying to right the ship so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 03-31-2017, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T04:17:46-07:00","id":1071174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1071170#post1071170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2309\" data-vbnamecard=\"2309\">Ashenrogue</a> you don't like the Idea and that is fine not every setting is for everyone. I am confident that I can prevent your &quot;Only Possible Outcome&quot; scenario without gutting the system. So we will just have to agree to disagree. Also there is not reason why there couldn't be a few places that a mage has embedded himself on a throne to rule or is the power behind the throne of a community. That scenario would be the exception not the rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, I'm saying that's the probable conclusion to such a thing. Like anything else it can be hand waived and said 'nah, that isn't how it happened'. It's just a logical path given the particular scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T04:33:51-07:00","id":1071181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1071044#post1071044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fairly sure I'd consider that gutting the magic system. As it stands I consider what we've got pretty much the ideal system of magic. It could probably be tuned slightly, but any change big enough to change the foreseen outcome is probably going to be enough to ruin it. I mean I'm sure some people wont mind, after all, some people like <i>vancian casting</i> for gods sake. But again, making it unreliable enough to matter is going to gut the system and take away part of what makes the mechanics of the gameline as good as it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gutting a system is when you take parts away or change it significantly, no one is talking about doing that. It's just adding another level of difficulty to using magic freely in much the same way that Sleepers and Paradox already do. From what Hardwire is saying it's not even a global problem, you just have to watch where you are.<br /> <br /> By the way Hardwire I'd consider adding a mobile threat that's immune to direct magical assault just so you can add that element of magical unreliability whenever you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 03-31-2017, 07:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T05:20:51-07:00","id":1071195,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2309\" data-vbnamecard=\"2309\">Ashenrogue</a> Understood and there is no reason that it couldn't turn out that way in a different setting, and yes there will be some hand waving involved, mainly with removing some of the arrogance of mages. They receive a blow to their arrogance when the destroyed the world. So the normal air of superiority that mages have will be tamed down.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> The hunters if they have a Null Device (Now I have named the portable dead zone) will be immune to direct magic. Some of the beasts, with their innate Paradox riddled forms, will mutate magic cast directly on them. I was thinking of some different magic storms and environments that can &quot;F&quot; with magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T05:43:22-07:00","id":1071200,"title":"","content":"Is dissonance still around in this setting?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, sans-serif\">Abyss Zones</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, sans-serif\"><br /> <br /> Wouldn't those be Abyssal Verges?</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T05:47:00-07:00","id":1071201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1071200#post1071200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is dissonance still around in this setting?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Wouldn't those be Abyssal Verges?[/FONT]</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and Abyssal Verge, just adding my own flare to the setting<br /> <br /> I haven't figured out how dissonance would work yet, I feel there would be some but how much of a factor is still a Mystery to me. <i><span style=\"color:#808080\">Failed my scrutiny on \u200bthis subject</span></i><br /> <br /> I don't want to say that everyone is at a sleepwalker level of awareness that magic exists but at the same time almost everyone is aware that there is some strange shit out there.<br /> <br /> One of my favorite setting out there is Gamma World and that is somewhat were I am heading with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 03-31-2017, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T06:42:16-07:00","id":1071223,"title":"","content":"There isn't a reason Sleepers can't know about magic, they're just harmed by directly witnessing it. <br /> <br /> I imagine something like a magical storm would be soul rending for Sleepers, paradoxically their witnessing it would also reduce its effects as Dissonance kicks in if they work sort of like normal Supernal phenomena.<br /> <br /> It feels to me like it would be a sort of post-apocalyptic version of the pre-Sundering Dark Era(Age?) of the People.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T06:46:48-07:00","id":1071224,"title":"","content":"Ya that is what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12191_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12191\" data-vbnamecard=\"12191\">Malus</a> Stated as well, and that makes alot of sense, just modify that to be Post-Apocalyptic instead per civilization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T10:24:53-07:00","id":1071313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1071223#post1071223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn't a reason Sleepers can't know about magic, they're just harmed by directly witnessing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're also harmed <i>again</i> by <i>remembering </i>it. Every time they remember it in fact. Which is why I originally assumed Dissonance and Quiescence were going to removed completely because it would make it almost impossible for the world to know and accept that mages caused the end of the world with their magic. That not being the case leads me to believe that we're just ignoring that part or something, otherwise just about every human in the world has had their Integrity fully eroded and likely driven hopelessly insane as the knowledge continuously carves up their mind/soul..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T11:54:30-07:00","id":1071356,"title":"","content":"Many humans maybe, but not necessarily all, and depending how long ago this apocalypse happened it's possible Sleepers have been making a comeback even if magic is widely known about.<br /> <br /> In some ways it's strange that Mages went into hiding in the first place, they didn't need to when they were with the People so there's this interesting question of why they decided to pull in and let only select groups of non-Mages know about them in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T12:32:00-07:00","id":1071370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1071356#post1071356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many humans maybe, but not necessarily all, and depending how long ago this apocalypse happened it's possible Sleepers have been making a comeback even if magic is widely known about.<br /> <br /> In some ways it's strange that Mages went into hiding in the first place, they didn't need to when they were with the People so there's this interesting question of why they decided to pull in and let only select groups of non-Mages know about them in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess whichever humans managed to either suppress their memories of the event psychologically rather than mystically or who never witnessed it and only heard about magic second hand through the raving madness of those who couldn't. But given that, there's little reason to believe something like magic and witches when they've literally never seen any magic (because Dissonance wont let them remember, and if it does they have no way to retain their Integrity), not seriously anyways. I mean they might form some sort of superstition that the destruction and madness were caused by magic, but with literally no person without degenerating Integrity ever being able to actually witness such a thing I don't see it <i>really </i>being held as true by the general populace. I guess it really depends on how Dissonance is changed in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T14:15:58-07:00","id":1071413,"title":"","content":"As I stated the general populace is somewhere between Sleeper and Sleepwalker, They know that there is some strange stuff happening and whether they believe that it is magic, technology or people being mutated by radiation fallout. I also stated that I do not know what I am doing with that part yet, this thought is not even a day old yet.<br /> <br /> We already know that you disagree with the setting idea and the it won't hold water.<br /> <br /> As for people not knowing about magic or they will be hurt by it, just read To the Strongest, it states in there that most everyone believed in sorcery but they have never seen it, but the belief is still there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T14:44:16-07:00","id":1071423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1071413#post1071413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I stated the general populace is somewhere between Sleeper and Sleepwalker, They know that there is some strange stuff happening and whether they believe that it is magic, technology or people being mutated by radiation fallout. I also stated that I do not know what I am doing with that part yet, this thought is not even a day old yet.<br /> <br /> We already know that you disagree with the setting idea and the it won't hold water.<br /> <br /> As for people not knowing about magic or they will be hurt by it, just read To the Strongest, it states in there that most everyone believed in sorcery but they have never seen it, but the belief is still there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't necessarily disagree with the idea, I just see a lot of holes that need to need to plugged for it to make sense. I don't mean that in a bad way, it's just you came seemingly looking for a critique and I'm giving you one. There are a lot of mechanics built into the system that make the setting you're proposing a bit sketchy and might be brought up in play, so I'm bringing attention to them now.<br /> <br /> And wasn't To the Strongest set back when such thoughts were the general truth of things as far as the populace knew? I assume that with your setting we're talking current modern day, where such things while held in superstition aren't <i>really</i> taken seriously by the population. So while they <i>can</i> believe it, due to the skeptical nature of todays people given the circumstances, I'd wager people are more likely to believe that terrorists or the Russians, or something like that did it <i>loooong</i> before they'll believe it was magic, <i>especially </i>since they'll never be able to see/remember proof of it, and all proof they see will always be remembered as something mundane.<br /> <br /> So unless the population is now made up of an outstandingly high number of Sleepwalkers (and why are there that many? Did the war, even with as much Paradox stuff is being thrown around in the setting, <i>really</i> free that many people from the Abyssal shard in their soul?) it just beggars belief that the general population would believe it was a bunch of <i>wizards</i> that ended the world. And again, you can hand waive it and just say that that is what they believe, but I feel that you should take note that it <i>is</i> something you might need to consider, and hopefully come up with an explanation for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T15:25:35-07:00","id":1071439,"title":"","content":"The Orders could step out and identify themselves, or at least the SL and FC might, and they don't have to claim responsibility just that they're Mages and they'll clean this mess up. After enough time of them not fulfilling that promise suspicion would turn to them. Before you say that won't work with Sleepers, I'd like to remind you that there are Sleepers currently in the employ of the Orders who know who they're working for. Now, there might be large chunks of the population that won't believe the Mages can actually do magic, but given enough time there will be a significant minority who will, and the rest will still see Mages as a force to be reckoned with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T16:25:09-07:00","id":1071483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1071439#post1071439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Orders could step out and identify themselves, or at least the SL and FC might, and they don't have to claim responsibility just that they're Mages and they'll clean this mess up. After enough time of them not fulfilling that promise suspicion would turn to them. Before you say that won't work with Sleepers, I'd like to remind you that there are Sleepers currently in the employ of the Orders who know who they're working for. Now, there might be large chunks of the population that won't believe the Mages can actually do magic, but given enough time there will be a significant minority who will, and the rest will still see Mages as a force to be reckoned with.</div> </div> </div> </div>And why would they step out and identify themselves though? They haven't done it for <i>how many</i> years? Dissonance hasn't changed, Paradox hasn't changed, nothings really changed other than that the world got worse and Abyssal crap is more prevalent than ever. Why, in such uncertain times, would they even attempt to tell Sleepers about magic, <i>especially</i> given the cause of the worlds current state? So that Sleepers can keep a closer eye on them and actively make it <i>harder</i> to fix the world when it is in a state where magic is <i>even more unreliable than usual</i>?<br /> <br /> Now I have no doubt a few will try to show the world that magic exists, just as I'm sure there's a few that try in the base setting, but why would it be any more effective now than it would before the end of the world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T22:14:57-07:00","id":1071618,"title":"","content":"It's not exactly what you are proposing but it might have ideas you can mine. Fantasy Flight Games put out a setting called Midnight that was a degree of post apocalypse caused when all souls were cut off from the afterlife, meaning zombie apocalypse and now we burn (or seal away) the dead.<br /> \u200bThere were two things that were specifically aimed at limiting mages in the setting.<br /> \u200bThe first, and I never actually bought the books so I can't remember what they were called, was a sort of hunting spirit that any use of magic (in your case probably Paradox) risked attracting. This spirit wasn't really that powerful but it couldn't be attacked or in any way effected directly. At the same time the only way it could effect the world was by possessing a weak willed host. The example I remember had a mage cast a spell in the wilderness, only to have that hawk lazily circling above suddenly come diving claws extended. He kills the hawk, only to have a chittering squirrel suddenly come leaping down from above, clawing at his face and eyes. He kills the squirrel, only to have a dear grazing in the next meadow come charging with antlers lowered. In the end the only thing he could do was kill its current host, then run and hope by the time it found another it had lost his trail. It could only see him through the eyes of host.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe second, thinking in terms of The Awakening, was that in the war the Seers and their Exarch patrons won. They then set up a theocracy modeled after the inquisition that hunted and executed anyone suspected of using magic. The Sleepers don't have to believe in magic, they just believe that they will be rewarded for turning in their neighbor (or strangers) while living in fear of the same being done to them. For Mages, if you accept being bound by the Iron Seals you can join the inquisition and live like royalty, but you do it knowing that at any time one of your rivals might succeed in turning that same inquisition on you (membership doesn't guarantee safety, not when politics are involved). If you don't join, then it is kill on sight and the rewards for helping are high.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6084,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","user":"2ptTakrill","date":". 04-01-2017, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T22:42:50-07:00","id":1071624,"title":"","content":"In terms of additional ChroD material that might benefit your setting.<br /> <br /> For ways to hunt Mages you might check out the supplement Witch Finders from Hunter: the Vigil. It is literally all about that. Heads up though, it uses 1e rules and also contradicts certain elements of Mage lore. You'll probably have better luck mining it for ideas than pulling stuff in directly.<br /> <br /> For representing post-apocalyptic landscapes ravaged by supernatural forces you might check out the Wasteland rules from Promethean: the Created (either 1e or 2e).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T06:03:35-07:00","id":1071690,"title":"","content":"Now then, I think I've talked about the little flaws long enough, so lets get down to actually making this setting work. First and foremost you might want to decide exactly how mages fucked up so hard to destroy the world and to more importantly to what <i>extent</i> and <i>why</i>? How thorough was the destruction? Was it world wide? Were any sections of the globe spared to where modern conveniences still thrive? And what/who were the mages fighting against to cause such widespread destruction, because to be apocalyptic in nature this had to be some high tier shit.<br /> <br /> Was it mostly the fault of the Exarchs? Did they feel that they were being pushed back too much and decided to hit the reset button on humanities progress seeing that if they can't blind them with opulence they'd blind them with deprivation? Or maybe the Scelesti all finally got their shit together and started working on some sort of Celestial Ladder to the Abyss or something and the fight was to stop them from completing it? It would explain the prevalence of all the Abyssal stuff roaming the wasteland now.<br /> <br /> As for the actual hazards, a lot of your proposed solutions to making the dangers of the wastelands hard to deal with seemed to be by making them Abyssal in nature, of which I agree with. I would suggest that whatever you choose to be the exact cause of all of this to be able to justify the sheer amount of Abyssal stuff here. Anyways, lets start with corrupted Abyssal beasts roaming the wastes. The Abyss represents everything that isn't and can't be, which encompasses a vast amount of stuff. I feel that that should be embraced, and that the beasts that monstrosities that roam the countryside should have such a large amount of varying abilities between them that you're never sure what one is going to be capable of if you run across one. They should probably be composed of <i>mostly</i> animals (maybe buildings or even elements) corrupted and warped by the Abyss, with the occasional pure Abyssal creature thrown in to shake things up.<br /> <br /> Now lets talk about this Abyss tainted mana. I'm thinking it should function like a lapsed Paradox Condition, causing all of their spells to have a base Paradox chance of 1 die. I'd also allow mages to scour that mana away with like they scour other things. Which brings me to another aspect of corrupted Abyssal creatures I'd suggest, and that is that they rarely, if ever, actively attack those with traces of the Abyss inside them. Which means that most Sleepers would be relatively safe from them unless they actively attempt to provoke them. The same applies to mages with tainted mana in their systems. This leads to mages <i>wanting</i> to have at least 1 point of corrupted mana in them in order to avoid detection by the monsters, even though it causes all of their spells to cause Paradox.<br /> <br /> Another thing I was tossing around is to let the Abyssal creatures have low innate Sympathy through Sleepers. Their Abyssal nature resonating with the shard in a Sleepers soul, making it to where Sleepers have a strange lack of fear/aversion to the monstrosities around them. I'm leaning towards them still <i>seeing</i> them as they are, but just not being able to find anything <i>wrong</i> about their appearance. I'd go as far as to say that Sleepers even take the smaller more manageable ones as <i>pets</i>. There should also be some sort of unseen negative effect, because the Abyss is pretty much never benign to anyone but I haven't quite thought of what yet. I've got a few more ideas but I'll get at those sometime later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T06:14:00-07:00","id":1071692,"title":"","content":"I like that last idea","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T07:10:18-07:00","id":1071708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1071690#post1071690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now then, I think I've talked about the little flaws long enough, so lets get down to actually making this setting work. First and foremost you might want to decide exactly how mages fucked up so hard to destroy the world and to more importantly to what <i>extent</i> and <i>why</i>? How thorough was the destruction? Was it world wide? Were any sections of the globe spared to where modern conveniences still thrive? And what/who were the mages fighting against to cause such widespread destruction, because to be apocalyptic in nature this had to be some high tier shit.<br /> <br /> Was it mostly the fault of the Exarchs? Did they feel that they were being pushed back too much and decided to hit the reset button on humanities progress seeing that if they can't blind them with opulence they'd blind them with deprivation? Or maybe the Scelesti all finally got their shit together and started working on some sort of Celestial Ladder to the Abyss or something and the fight was to stop them from completing it? It would explain the prevalence of all the Abyssal stuff roaming the wasteland now.<br /> <br /> As for the actual hazards, a lot of your proposed solutions to making the dangers of the wastelands hard to deal with seemed to be by making them Abyssal in nature, of which I agree with. I would suggest that whatever you choose to be the exact cause of all of this to be able to justify the sheer amount of Abyssal stuff here. Anyways, lets start with corrupted Abyssal beasts roaming the wastes. The Abyss represents everything that isn't and can't be, which encompasses a vast amount of stuff. I feel that that should be embraced, and that the beasts that monstrosities that roam the countryside should have such a large amount of varying abilities between them that you're never sure what one is going to be capable of if you run across one. They should probably be composed of <i>mostly</i> animals (maybe buildings or even elements) corrupted and warped by the Abyss, with the occasional pure Abyssal creature thrown in to shake things up.<br /> <br /> Now lets talk about this Abyss tainted mana. I'm thinking it should function like a lapsed Paradox Condition, causing all of their spells to have a base Paradox chance of 1 die. I'd also allow mages to scour that mana away with like they scour other things. Which brings me to another aspect of corrupted Abyssal creatures I'd suggest, and that is that they rarely, if ever, actively attack those with traces of the Abyss inside them. Which means that most Sleepers would be relatively safe from them unless they actively attempt to provoke them. The same applies to mages with tainted mana in their systems. This leads to mages <i>wanting</i> to have at least 1 point of corrupted mana in them in order to avoid detection by the monsters, even though it causes all of their spells to cause Paradox.<br /> <br /> Another thing I was tossing around is to let the Abyssal creatures have low innate Sympathy through Sleepers. Their Abyssal nature resonating with the shard in a Sleepers soul, making it to where Sleepers have a strange lack of fear/aversion to the monstrosities around them. I'm leaning towards them still <i>seeing</i> them as they are, but just not being able to find anything <i>wrong</i> about their appearance. I'd go as far as to say that Sleepers even take the smaller more manageable ones as <i>pets</i>. There should also be some sort of unseen negative effect, because the Abyss is pretty much never benign to anyone but I haven't quite thought of what yet. I've got a few more ideas but I'll get at those sometime later.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of these points have merit and I was struggling with the Why of it all. I like the Scelesti as that does play into the whole Abyssal theme. I was thinking that there would be a few Cities spared the Apocalypse and they would be Dead Zones. I was thinking that the same thing about the Abyssal Beasts atleast the part about no two alike and a pure Abyssal being every now and then. I would like to give Abyss Tainted Mana a little more teeth than just 1 die of Paradox especially if having it would shield you from the Abyssal Beasts. Unless what you were saying by a Base 1 die of Paradox that cannot be mitigated with Dedicated Magic Tools or Mana, then that is a significant punch, I was actually rethinking the 1 Paradox per tainted Mana and going with the Gnosis generated Paradox to all spells and the Paradox could not be mitigated.<br /> <br /> The Sympathy with the sleepers is a cool idea. and as for pets &quot;Have you seen my pet Targ&quot; springs to mind.<br /> <br /> There was a second setting that sprang to mid with all the talk about Sleepers and that would be that the Normal world was unaffected and the desolation was on a Supernal level. The wasteland is where the Nodes and Hallows became corrupted or just disappeared. But I think that might still affect the world as a whole for the sleepers because if I remember correctly the Layline and Nodes actually represent the world flow of energy and bring stability to the nature of the planet, I could be wrong there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T08:17:04-07:00","id":1071716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1071708#post1071708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All of these points have merit and I was struggling with the Why of it all. I like the Scelesti as that does play into the whole Abyssal theme. I was thinking that there would be a few Cities spared the Apocalypse and they would be Dead Zones. I was thinking that the same thing about the Abyssal Beasts atleast the part about no two alike and a pure Abyssal being every now and then. I would like to give Abyss Tainted Mana a little more teeth than just 1 die of Paradox especially if having it would shield you from the Abyssal Beasts. Unless what you were saying by a Base 1 die of Paradox that cannot be mitigated with Dedicated Magic Tools or Mana, then that is a significant punch, I was actually rethinking the 1 Paradox per tainted Mana and going with the Gnosis generated Paradox to all spells and the Paradox could not be mitigated.<br /> <br /> The Sympathy with the sleepers is a cool idea. and as for pets &quot;Have you seen my pet Targ&quot; springs to mind.<br /> <br /> There was a second setting that sprang to mid with all the talk about Sleepers and that would be that the Normal world was unaffected and the desolation was on a Supernal level. The wasteland is where the Nodes and Hallows became corrupted or just disappeared. But I think that might still affect the world as a whole for the sleepers because if I remember correctly the Layline and Nodes actually represent the world flow of energy and bring stability to the nature of the planet, I could be wrong there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well like all Paradox, it builds with every spell cast in a scene. So even if you reduce it to a chance die for the first cast, the second cast it goes up by 1 and so on, and this isn't even counting any Paradox dice added unto by excess Reach, Sleeper witnesses, etc. Just that by itself gets really nasty really quickly in any situation in which they have to cast more than 1 or 2 spell within a scene. Though if it does turn out to be a little too weak for your liking you'd be free to have it ignore things like Dedicated Tools and the like. That said, I feel that 1 die of Paradox per point of tainted mana is way too heavy handed. I feel that at that point your players might just say fuck magic altogether, and magic is kinda the point of the game. <br /> <br /> As for nodes and the like, I'm not read up on those enough to be comfortable saying either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 04-01-2017, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T12:04:05-07:00","id":1071777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1071483#post1071483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And why would they step out and identify themselves though? They haven't done it for <i>how many</i> years? Dissonance hasn't changed, Paradox hasn't changed, nothings really changed other than that the world got worse and Abyssal crap is more prevalent than ever. Why, in such uncertain times, would they even attempt to tell Sleepers about magic?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was imagining a scenario in which things have been upended enough that Mages would feel the need to step out of secrecy in order to extend an umbrella of protection from those circumstances as far as possible, or attempt to create safe points to gather at. Yeah, the dangers from Sleepers hasn't changed, but the dangers to Sleepers have grown to the extent that continuing to hide does more harm than good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T12:18:10-07:00","id":1071779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1071777#post1071777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was imagining a scenario in which things have been upended enough that Mages would feel the need to step out of secrecy in order to extend an umbrella of protection from those circumstances as far as possible, or attempt to create safe points to gather at. Yeah, the dangers from Sleepers hasn't changed, but the dangers to Sleepers have grown to the extent that continuing to hide does more harm than good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Similar to the Neolithic? 'I can help, but you can't stay to witness it.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-01-2017, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T19:26:02-07:00","id":1071867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070875-mage-the-desolation?p=1071777#post1071777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was imagining a scenario in which things have been upended enough that Mages would feel the need to step out of secrecy in order to extend an umbrella of protection from those circumstances as far as possible, or attempt to create safe points to gather at. Yeah, the dangers from Sleepers hasn't changed, but the dangers to Sleepers have grown to the extent that continuing to hide does more harm than good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just don't see how revealing themselves to Sleepers is supposed to help with this. Fine, you want to extend the umbrella of protection as far as possible and attempt to create safe places to gather at. Fine. Letting them know you can use magic seems to actively hurt such an effort imo. They then start to pay closer attention to those efforts, no longer thinking it was mere coincidence or impressive skill and begin seeing it for the magic that it is, unraveling your spells while simultaneously harming their souls. They'd be so much better off wandering around doing it in secret, making them believe that it was just through luck that an area was spared the destruction the rest of the world had suffered.<br /> <br /> When monsters stop roaming near due to warding spells they don't look at a monster outside roam past them without seeming to notice and think, this must be the effect of that magic we were told about and then suffer for it. They'd think, there must be something about this area that they don't like, maybe a plant of some kind whose smell they can't tolerate. When people working on rebuilding shelters suddenly begin lifting heavier objects and tire slower they won't think, the blessing of that shaman really works, and suffer from Dissonance. They'll go, this seems much easier than last time, I must be getting stronger/better at this. <br /> <br /> Long story short, I <i>still</i> see nothing but disadvantages in telling people about mages being a thing. There's risk but not really any reward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T03:27:50-07:00","id":1071969,"title":"","content":"When I get a handle on what role the Sleepers will play in this and just how much they know then I will post it, for right now lets just say that they know something went on and that an undisclosed group caused it. My thoughts at the moment is that their overall consciousness has been raised to a level where less things make them reach a breaking point. The populace as a whole will believe what they believe until proven otherwise, it could be something as simple as a weaker form of Delirium where there minds try to explain away what they saw and until magic is shoved down their throats (the actual subject of a spell not just seeing it) they don't have a breaking point. They may not know what went on or how it was done but they know you did it and that they need to call the Hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}